For `expanded` on the chip, I'll add `static classes = [ "deleteable", "deleting", "expanded" ]` → attributes `data-reaction-deleteable-class="reaction--deleteable"`, `data-reaction-deleting-class="reaction--deleting"`, `data-reaction-expanded-class="expanded"`.

Hmm, that's 3 data attributes per chip — verbose in the partial. Alternative: since these class names come from the shipped CSS (reaction--deleteable, reaction--deleting) and `expanded`, maybe hardcode them in the controller as constants? Hardcoding CSS class names in JS is not great but the CSS is "design-shipped" and stable... The repo's `notifications_controller.js` uses `static classes`/values. Let me check another controller to see how they handle CSS class names — e.g. `bubble_controller.js` or `bar_controller.js`.

